  "provider_query": "CPython source file that defines PyObject_Malloc",
  "answer": "**`PyObject_Malloc` is defined in `Objects/obmalloc.c`.**\n\nIt is the public object-domain allocator. The body checks the size against `PY_SSIZE_T_MAX` and then calls the current object allocator (`_PyObject.malloc`). The pymalloc implementation lives in the same file as the internal `_PyObject_Malloc` (when `WITH_PYMALLOC` is on).\n\nRelevant sources (up to 8):\n\n1. **Definition** — `Objects/obmalloc.c` (current and older tags, e.g. 3.12): `void * PyObject_Malloc(size_t size)` dispatches to `_PyObject.malloc`.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Objects/obmalloc.c  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/v3.12.0/Objects/obmalloc.c\n\n2. **Declaration** — `Include/objimpl.h`: `PyAPI_FUNC(void *) PyObject_Malloc(size_t size);` with notes that it uses Python’s small-block allocator.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Include/objimpl.h\n\n3. **Docs** — `Doc/c-api/memory.rst`: allocates *n* bytes in the object domain; zero bytes may return a distinct non-NULL pointer; GIL / attached thread state required.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Doc/c-api/memory.rst\n\n4. **Internal allocator overview** — `Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h`: object allocator layer used by `PyObject_New` / `Del` unless a type has its own scheme.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h\n\n5. **Domain enum** — `Include/pymem.h`: `PYMEM_DOMAIN_OBJ` covers `PyObject_Malloc` / `Realloc` / `Free`.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Include/pymem.h\n\n6. **Call site example** — `Objects/object.c`: variable-size object allocation via `PyObject_Malloc`.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Objects/object.c\n\n7. **Docs that mention the call** — `Doc/c-api/allocation.rst`: `PyObject_New` allocates with `PyObject_Malloc` then initializes like `PyObject_Init`.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Doc/c-api/allocation.rst\n\n8. **Free-threaded path** — `Include/internal/pycore_object_alloc.h`: `_PyObject_MallocWithType` selects a mimalloc heap then calls `PyObject_Malloc`.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Include/internal/pycore_object_alloc.h",
